//! End-to-end TC/ CACHED-PATH STITCHING (thread R2-C): Rust source -> stage1
//! MIR -> trust-ir frontend closure emit -> trust-cg JIT -> native == JIT
//! differential. De-models the two skeptic-flagged round-1 boundaries:
//!
//!   (1) infer_proj's is_prop ERR-PROPAGATION GATE (clean-kernel
//!       tc/infer_proj.rs:95, #2208): the full infer_proj_type_from_impl is
//!       transcribed VERBATIM — the top proj_type_cache consult, the
//!       `let is_prop_type = self.is_prop(&expr_type_whnf)?;` gate, the
//!       non-Prop batch fill, the strict Prop-validating batch fill (whose
//!       per-field `if !self.is_prop(&domain)?` is a SECOND propagation
//!       site), the quick-path walk, and is_prop itself — and verified
//!       native == JIT on Ok paths AND on two genuine Err-propagation paths
//!       (an undeclared struct type; an undeclared Prop-field type), with
//!       the Err IDENTITY (variant + payload) compared exactly. The negative
//!       control is a GATE-SWALLOWING corrupted oracle (the pre-#2208 bug:
//!       `is_prop(..).unwrap_or(false)`) which must DISAGREE with the JIT.
//!
//!   (2) the cached whnf_core ROUTING (tc/whnf.rs / tc/whnf_proj.rs):
//!       whnf_impl's already-normal kind gate, whnf_inner's whnf_cache
//!       hit/miss/record routing, whnf_outer_loop's mid-loop consult on the
//!       delta-unfolded intermediate (#3210), whnf_recurse /
//!       whnf_core_no_delta's whnf_core_cache read-UNCONDITIONAL /
//!       write-only-full-proj discipline (#1768, Lean 4 `!cheap_rec &&
//!       !cheap_proj`) — at BOTH write sites: the whnf_core_no_delta gate
//!       (s5) and the whnf_recurse gate, whose polarity is pinned by the s9
//!       cheap-only probe (core cache must stay EMPTY; closes the round-2
//!       skeptic's falsifiability gap) —, reduce_proj's cross-mode escalation into FULL cached
//!       whnf, and unfold_definition_cached's only-successes m_unfold cache —
//!       verified by cold / warm / POISONED-cache runs (a wrong cached value
//!       must be OBSERVED identically by native and JIT, proving the machine
//!       code actually consults the caches), plus cache-length packing as a
//!       record-effect differential. The CACHES themselves stay modeled
//!       (assoc-list over Vec<(Expr, Expr)> with the REAL transcribed
//!       Expr::eq key discipline — hashbrown is out of scope; boundary [C3]
//!       in the slice).
//!
//! The embedded consts are the byte-verbatim `--mir-emit-closure` outputs over
//! the R2-C session slice `clean_tc_stitch_slice.rs` (in-repo copy at
//! tests/slices/clean_tc_stitch_slice.rs; every modeled boundary documented
//! inline as [C1]-[C11]). Both emitted with validate_module = 0 error(s),
//! re-parse OK; re-emits verified byte-identical before embedding.
//!
//! REGEN:
//!   S=$HOME/trust/build/aarch64-apple-darwin/stage1
//!   cd $HOME/trust-ir/frontend && env -u RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN RUSTC=$S/bin/rustc \
//!     DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH=$S/lib/rustlib/aarch64-apple-darwin/lib \
//!     $S/bin/cargo run --bin trust_ir_mir -- <abs>/clean_tc_stitch_slice.rs \
//!       --crate-type=lib --mir-emit-closure tc_proj_root <out1.tir>
//!   (and --mir-emit-closure tc_whnf_route_root <out2.tir>)
//!
//! RUN ONE TEST AT A TIME (JIT module-accumulation SIGTRAPs a full-suite
//! single process; see jit-parallel-race-2026-06-29.md):
//!   cargo test -p trust-cg-codegen --test e2e_tc_stitching -- --exact \
//!     mir_tc_infer_proj_gate_err_propagation_roundtrip --test-threads=1

